   "html_text": "Parfit illustrates the no-difference view by considering two medical programs (1984: 367). In both programs, a rare condition can be passed from mother to child. One involves pregnancy testing: if the test is positive, fetuses are treated for the rare condition. The other involves preconception testing: women who test positive as carriers of the rare condition are advised to postpone conception for at least two months and to undergo a harmless treatment, after which the condition will have disap",
